{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792507888,"nonce":"Z3PVERc+4WlgrY2QSLg9OI4fNqk=","message":"Initial offscreen controls failed before implementation. A quarter-turn image left blue at (75,27), where the independent inverse-affine reference expected yellow. A sheared image's grouped scratch bounds were [51.33542,37.22361,53.329163,35.552773] instead of [34,26,88,58]. Log: /private/tmp/blinc-rgba-affine-negative.log.\n\nRaw RGBA now retains the normalized centered local affine that transform_rect's determinant-scaled destination requires. DynamicImage carries this matrix; the existing image instance consumes it. Ordered bounds use the transformed quad, tight bakes translate its center and clip into the layer frame, and scratch fingerprints include the matrix. Non-finite, overflowed, empty or near-singular geometry is rejected before pixel allocation/GPU upload. No primitive or image-instance GPU layout changed.\n\nAn additional post-producer control proved the image shader's 0.0001 identity tolerance drops valid small shears on large quads: (19,60) became red instead of blue (/private/tmp/blinc-rgba-affine-small-negative.log). Both generated native image shader variants now apply every non-identity matrix. This is a local vertex condition change, not shader fork generation/redesign.\n\nFive normal GPU cases and one CPU hash case now pass. They compare asymmetric RGBA texels against an independent inverse-affine reference for rotation, shear, reflection, non-uniform scale and DPI transforms in background and foreground; check transformed scratch bounds and tight opacity bakes; test near-identity shear; check image-only motion, rectangular clip, 4x MSAA, overlay, glass and reduced-backdrop frame translations; reject invalid manually supplied geometry; and exercise three changing-orientation frames in all three application entry points. New CPU cases cover active owners, corner mapping, composed DPI/translation, reflected axes, bounds and invalid geometry. Capability sweep and full gate pending.\n\nShaped raw-image clipping, general cross-stream isolation, prepared text/SVG/ImageElement streams and named Sample remain outside the slice. Browser/mobile pixels and timing/memory benchmarks are unverified.","files":null}]}